   "peak_elev": null,
   "parent": "Whitney & Surrounding Peaks",
   "pitches": 0,
   "approach": null,
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "Retrace the trail from the summit: follow it south to Trail Crest, then drop east past Trail Camp, Consultation Lake, Outpost Camp and Lone Pine Lake to Whitney Portal, over six thousand feet below the summit. The trail is usually clear of snow from midsummer to early autumn. In spring and early summer, snow and ice linger on the upper switchbacks, and an axe and crampons are needed for the descent as for the climb. A permit is required year-round for the Whitney Zone.",
